.TH MKPASS-GUI 1 "July 2026" "mkpass 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkpass-gui \- Qt graphical interface for mkpass password generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkpass-gui
[\fIQT_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkpass-gui
is the graphical Qt user interface for the
.B mkpass
stateless password and passphrase generator.
.PP
It provides an intuitive visual interface to regenerate strong passwords on-demand using a \fBMaster Password\fR and a \fBService Name\fR.
.PP
Key Features of the GUI:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBReal-time Service Autocomplete\fR: Instant suggestions derived from the local SQLite database.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInteractive Controls\fR: Dynamic form controls for algorithm selection (Argon2, SHA512, Diceware, WordNet pattern), length adjustments, and character set toggles.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDatabase Management Dialog\fR: Built-in manager accessible via the Database menu to view, search, and delete saved service configurations.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBClipboard Security\fR: Instant clipboard copy button with automatic clipboard wiping upon application shutdown.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIntegrated Help Manual\fR: Comprehensive user manual accessible directly from the Help menu.

.SH OPTIONS
.B mkpass-gui
accepts standard Qt command-line options:
.TP
\fB\-style\fR \fISTYLE\fR
Specify the Qt GUI style (e.g., fusion, breeze, cleanlooks).
.TP
\fB\-geometry\fR \fIGEOMETRY\fR
Set the main window size and position.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display standard command-line help options.

.SH USE CASES
.TP
.B Standard Desktop Password Generation
1. Launch \fBmkpass-gui\fR.
2. Type your Master Password in the password field.
3. Type or select a Service Name (e.g. "github.com").
4. Adjust options if required (algorithm, length, character sets).
5. Click \fBGenerate\fR or press Enter.
6. Click \fBCopy to Clipboard\fR.

.TP
.B Managing Stored Service Configurations
1. Open the \fBDatabase\fR menu and select \fBManagement\fR.
2. Search or browse saved service entries.
3. Select and delete obsolete service configurations.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkpass/config.db
SQLite database storing local non-secret service configuration entries and options history.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkpass (1)
